  "operative_text": "RESOLVED (lines 49-51): NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE SENATE that the members of this body condemn the killing of Alex Pretti, and condemn the killing of any American citizen where the asserted justification is the lawful exercise of constitutional rights.\nRESOLVED (lines 55-57): BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the Senate calls upon all elected officials, regardless of party affiliation, to reject rhetoric that equates peaceful protest or lawful firearm possession with criminality or terrorism.\nRESOLVED (lines 58-62): BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the members of this body commit to working together to protect the constitutional rights of peaceful assembly and the right to keep and bear arms, as guaranteed under both state and federal law, from encroachment or abuse by federal immigration law enforcement agencies that have demonstrated a pattern of disregard for the civil liberties of American citizens."
}